apply to third-party datasets.

In particular, the Jordà--Schularick--Taylor Macrohistory Database is provided
under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and is not covered by the IdSS MIT licence. Fernald's TFP
data, used in `USsentiment`, may be reproduced with attribution for
noncommercial purposes. Other data have the source-specific terms recorded in
the dataset register.

USmonetaryRR is an extraction of the official Jorda--Taylor replication data
under CC0 1.0; it retains the extended Romer--Romer instrument and public-sector
macroeconomic inputs. Preserve source and scholarly credits. The licence and
provenance record are installed in data-sources/USmonetaryRR/.

See DATA-SOURCES.md in the installed package for the dataset-by-dataset audit.
